==Galician==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|gl|roa-opt|novo}}, from {{inh|gl|la|novus}}, from {{inh|gl|ine-pro|*néwos}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gl|[ˈnɔ.βʊ]|[ˈno.βʊ]}}

===Noun===
{{gl-noun|m}}

# {{lb|gl|usually|in the plural}} the [[young]] people
#: {{uxi|gl|Algúns vellos pensan que '''os novos''' só queren estar de troula|Some old people think that '''youngsters''' just want to have fun}}
# {{lb|gl|usually|in the plural}} the [[new]] produce of a field or farm

===Adjective===
{{gl-adj|f=nova}}

# [[new]]
#: {{ux|gl|O '''novo''' ministro prometeu o seu cargo.|The '''new''' minister promised his position.}}
# [[young]]
# [[freshly]] [[made]]
# [[brand new]]
# [[good as new]]
# belonging to the last [[harvest]]
#* {{quote-book|gl|year=1301|editor=X. Ferro Couselo|title=A vida e a fala dos devanceiros. Escolma de documentos en galego dos séculos XIII ao XVI|location=Vigo|publisher=Galaxia|page=52
|passage=''A Eluira, I moyo de pan do ''nouo'', de qual ouueren, e I bacoro''
|translation=To Elvira, one modius of grain of the '''new''' [harvest], whatever species they happen to have there, and one piglet}}

