==Portuguese==

===Etymology===
{{inh+|pt|roa-opt|novo}}, from {{inh|pt|la|novus|5=new}}, from {{inh|pt|itc-pro|*nowos}}, from {{inh|pt|ine-pro|*néwos||new}}. Compare {{cog|gl|novo}} and {{cog|es|nuevo}}.

===Pronunciation===
{{pt-IPA|nôvo}}
* {{a|Porto}} {{IPA|pt|[ˈnwɐ.βu]}}
* {{a|Rural Central Brazil}} {{IPA|pt|/ˈno.vʷ/}}
* {{audio|pt|Pt novo.ogg|Audio}}
* {{hyphenation|pt|no|vo}}

===Adjective===
{{pt-adj|meta=1|sup=+abs}}

# {{lb|pt|of things}} [[new]]
## recently made or created
##: {{ux|pt|É uma casa '''nova'''.|t=It is a '''new''' house.}}
## not previously worn or used
##: {{ux|pt|Comprei um carro '''novo'''.|t=I bought a '''new''' car.}}
#: {{syn|pt|novo em folha}}
## recently discovered
##: {{ux|pt|As '''novas''' ruínas vão ser úteis para os arqueólogos.|t=The '''new''' ruins will be useful to archaeologists.}}
## {{lb|pt|of a period of time|often follows the noun}} [[new]] {{gloss|about to begin or recently begun}}
##: {{ux|pt|Ano '''novo'''.|t='''New''' year.}}
# {{lb|pt|of persons or sometimes animals}} [[young]]
#: {{ux|pt|Ele é demasiado '''novo''' para assistir isso.|t=He is too '''young''' to watch this.}}
#: {{ux|pt|Ela é a minha irmã mais '''nova'''.|She is my '''youngest''' sister.}}
#: {{syn|pt|jovem|novato}}
# [[original]] {{gloss|fresh; different}}
#: {{ux|pt|Ideias '''novas''' para tempos novos.|t='''Original''' ideas for new times.}}
#: {{syn|pt|original}}

====Antonyms====
* {{sense|recently made or created}} {{l|pt|antigo}}, {{l|pt|velho}}, {{l|pt|vetusto}}
* {{sense|not previously worn or used}} {{l|pt|usado}}
* {{sense|young}} {{l|pt|idoso}}, {{l|en|velho}}
* {{sense|original}} {{l|pt|antigo}}, {{l|pt|antiquado}}, {{l|pt|ultrapassado}}, {{l|pt|vetusto}}
* {{sense|about to begin or recently begun}} {{l|pt|passado}}, {{l|pt|velho}}

